WEBVTT

00:01:25.270 --> 00:01:27.940
<i>The time is one hundred years ago.</i>

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:30.940
<i>Nadia is still selfish even on the desert island</i>

00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:33.860
<i>where they have started their new life.</i>

00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:39.450
<i>Early in the morning, she forced Jean and Marie to tour the island</i>

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:43.290
<i>naming the places and the animals her own way.</i>

00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:46.960
<i>Finally, she said that she was a new girl now.</i>

00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:52.050
<i>Nadia then went off into the jungle on her own</i>

00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:55.920
<i>to sever her connections with science and civilization.</i>

00:01:56.920 --> 00:02:02.560
<i>However, she has found it impossible to live alone in nature,</i>

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:06.060
<i>and she has decided to go back to Jean and Marie's place.</i>

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:11.860
<i>They have been reconciled, but has Nadia's selfish behavior changed?</i>

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:16.070
<i>What is she really thinking?</i>

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:28.710
Why did you use meat?

00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:30.420
How can you tell?

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:32.380
I can tell even if you chop it up!

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:34.340
How did you find it?

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:37.220
I can taste it!

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:38.550
It's delicious!

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:41.260
The problem isn't the taste!

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:42.800
Why did you use meat?

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:47.270
This is an emergency situation!
Don't be so selfish!

00:02:47.270 --> 00:02:49.270
I'm not selfish!

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:50.520
It's my policy!

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:52.480
Policy?

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:57.320
It's awful to eat a dead animal!
No human being should do that!

00:02:57.740 --> 00:03:00.660
It's not a dead animal. It's the food called meat.

00:03:01.070 --> 00:03:04.910
You mixed it in the omelet to hide it!

00:03:04.910 --> 00:03:06.870
Why did you try to deceive me?

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:08.870
I didn't deceive you.

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:12.750
It's good for you. Nutritious!
It strengthens your body.

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:16.670
You're cruel to kill animals to eat just for your nutrition.

00:03:16.670 --> 00:03:21.930
It's not just human beings. Most animals do it to live too.

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:23.220
You're a liar!

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:25.220
I am not! It's true!

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:27.470
Science proves it!

00:03:27.470 --> 00:03:31.190
Science! I knew it! That's why I can't believe in science!

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:35.860
It's phony! What you say is phony too!

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:39.280
But man has been eating meat since the beginning of time,

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:41.490
to grow strong and multiply.

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:43.320
So, the number of evil people increases?

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:45.320
That's complete nonsense!

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:49.290
You become evil by eating meat!

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:50.410
Oh, geez!

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:54.830
You'll become as evil as Jean if you keep eating meat.

00:03:54.830 --> 00:03:56.540
So stop eating it!

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:58.250
What a waste!

00:03:58.250 --> 00:04:00.630
It's you who are wasteful!

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:03.050
You waste the lives of animals.

00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:05.640
It's a waste if you don't eat now!

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:06.760
That's not true!

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:08.810
You'll get sick easily if you don't eat meat.

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:11.850
You might even die without the nutrition it provides.

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:14.520
I don't need that kind of nutrition!

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:16.810
You'll become an evil person if you eat nutritious food.

00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:20.030
You're wrong! Look at Marie and me...

00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:23.240
You're an evil boy because you deceived me.

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:26.280
You'll become a bad girl soon, Marie.

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:31.250
Why do you call me an evil boy?
I've been very worried about you.

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:36.460
You're trying to make me bad too by making me eat meat.

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:38.460
You must eat it, or you'll die.

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:41.670
But I can't! I can't eat an omelet with meat in it. It's sickening!

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:45.130
A plain omelet will do for me!

00:04:47.090 --> 00:04:47.890
What?

00:04:48.140 --> 00:04:50.140
Sickening?

00:04:52.430 --> 00:04:54.520
Wait a minute...

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:07.410
That's funny. You can eat eggs.

00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:08.410
That's right.

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:11.990
You know that eggs are born from hens, of course.

00:05:11.990 --> 00:05:13.450
Of course.

00:05:13.450 --> 00:05:15.920
An egg is a living thing before it is born.

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:18.710
An egg is an egg. It's not an animal yet.

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:23.260
I'll eat this if you won't.

00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:27.300
No, don't eat it. This is Nadia's.
She must eat it.

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:28.720
But I'm sure she won't.

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:31.220
That's right. I don't want anything!

00:05:31.220 --> 00:05:33.980
Really? You really don't want anything?

00:05:33.980 --> 00:05:40.360
Right! Man can live a week or two without eating or drinking.

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:42.070
So, you don't need water either?

00:05:42.070 --> 00:05:42.820
No!

00:05:42.820 --> 00:05:44.740
Marie will eat it!

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:47.820
Don't make complaints later!

00:05:47.820 --> 00:05:51.120
Never! I'll never do that!

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:55.080
You really are stubborn. You've gone too far to retreat.

00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:56.410
I'm not about to!

00:05:56.410 --> 00:06:00.000
I really mean it when I say I can go a week without eating!

00:06:17.730 --> 00:06:22.110
You really should have eaten something, Nadia.

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:25.940
A week hasn't passed yet. I'm not hungry at all.

00:06:27.070 --> 00:06:29.320
Give me the meat, Jean.

00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:32.530
There's not much left now.

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:37.120
I'm so hungry that it vanishes in no time.

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:40.920
You should eat some too, Nadia. It'll be okay.

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:45.250
No, thanks! Don't show me that corpse of an animal!

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:49.880
I hate those who eat meat!

00:06:53.050 --> 00:06:53.760
Nadia...

00:06:54.220 --> 00:06:55.510
I'm so hungry.

00:06:57.430 --> 00:07:01.230
What an insulting girl, just because she doesn't like meat.

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:18.660
Nadia...

00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:20.080
It tastes good, doesn't it?

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:22.790
I want to eat a lot of meat.

00:07:23.210 --> 00:07:26.630
I'll never eat an animal's dead body.

00:07:32.260 --> 00:07:35.550
What's wrong? I can't catch anything today.

00:07:36.470 --> 00:07:38.520
Maybe the bait's no good.

00:07:39.140 --> 00:07:41.980
Or are there no fish around here?

00:07:41.980 --> 00:07:43.940
That can't be it.

00:07:49.240 --> 00:07:52.570
Are we going to be eaten by sharks?

00:07:52.570 --> 00:07:56.030
I haven't done anything bad enough to deserve this!

00:07:56.910 --> 00:07:59.330
How terrible!

00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:02.960
Sanson! Wake up! Do something!

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:06.840
Seniorita, I am awake now!

00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:08.960
Go to hell, sharks!

00:08:13.590 --> 00:08:15.760
Bravo!

00:08:26.190 --> 00:08:27.770
Still nothing?

00:08:27.770 --> 00:08:29.440
Just a second.

00:08:32.990 --> 00:08:34.490
Ready!

00:08:45.290 --> 00:08:46.630
Marie, here's some water.

00:08:46.630 --> 00:08:49.090
You're so sweet to me.

00:08:49.090 --> 00:08:50.550
What are you saying?

00:08:50.550 --> 00:08:52.590
Thanks so much.

00:08:55.800 --> 00:08:59.510
That was good. You and Nadia can drink the rest.

00:08:59.510 --> 00:09:02.890
That's okay. Don't worry about us.

00:09:03.430 --> 00:09:06.230
I'm sorry to have troubled you.

00:09:06.230 --> 00:09:08.860
This is so you can hurry up and get better.

00:09:08.860 --> 00:09:10.270
That's your duty now, Marie.

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:11.320
Okay!

00:09:12.030 --> 00:09:14.860
I'll catch a big fish today.

00:09:14.860 --> 00:09:16.700
I'll be waiting, Darling.

00:09:16.700 --> 00:09:18.240
Oh, stop it.

00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:20.280
Nadia...

00:09:20.280 --> 00:09:24.660
You go fishing, and I'll collect water at the beach. Okay?

00:09:25.160 --> 00:09:27.120
Okay. Are you still angry?

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:28.830
No, I'm not.

00:09:29.210 --> 00:09:30.290
Are you sure?

00:09:30.290 --> 00:09:31.250
Yes, I'm sure.

00:09:31.420 --> 00:09:32.210
Really?

00:09:32.210 --> 00:09:33.170
Really!

00:09:34.630 --> 00:09:37.840
What? Do you want to make me angry?

00:09:38.340 --> 00:09:39.300
Of course not.

00:09:39.640 --> 00:09:43.600
Why don't you go, then? To kill the fish!

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:48.520
Why does she get so angry?

00:09:49.980 --> 00:09:52.440
Maybe she's too hungry.

00:09:54.190 --> 00:09:56.860
But she gets angry even if she's not hungry.

00:09:58.320 --> 00:10:02.580
I don't have the strength to get angry, because I'm too hungry.

00:10:14.460 --> 00:10:15.970
This takes too much time.

00:10:20.180 --> 00:10:21.640
It's so hot!

00:10:27.890 --> 00:10:31.440
Just this much for all this waiting?

00:10:37.280 --> 00:10:39.700
This thing is unfair too!

00:10:41.780 --> 00:10:43.370
Don't get away now!

00:10:44.830 --> 00:10:46.370
I got it!

00:10:50.920 --> 00:10:52.040
Spinach!

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:13.730
Thanks for the food!

00:11:15.940 --> 00:11:17.690
I took the ink out.

00:11:17.690 --> 00:11:19.700
This is so delicious!

00:11:22.700 --> 00:11:24.620
Why don't you have some, Nadia?

00:11:27.410 --> 00:11:29.290
No thanks.

00:11:49.270 --> 00:11:51.690
Wow! This feels so good!

00:11:51.890 --> 00:11:55.900
Go collect more cans to catch water, Marie!

00:11:55.900 --> 00:11:56.860
Okay!

00:11:57.900 --> 00:11:59.110
Where's Nadia?

00:11:59.400 --> 00:12:00.820
She's sleeping.

00:12:01.110 --> 00:12:04.820
It's a waste of time to sleep now.

00:12:06.780 --> 00:12:09.290
Marie, did you eat any of Gargoyle's canned food?

00:12:09.450 --> 00:12:11.370
No, I haven't.

00:12:11.370 --> 00:12:14.750
I thought I threw this away because the inside was rotten.

00:12:14.750 --> 00:12:15.710
King, perhaps?

00:12:17.380 --> 00:12:21.380
But he's always been at the cliffs these days.

00:12:21.880 --> 00:12:23.470
Spinach?

00:12:24.470 --> 00:12:25.550
It's Nadia!

00:12:27.550 --> 00:12:28.810
Nadia, are you all right?

00:12:28.810 --> 00:12:29.770
What are you talking about?

00:12:29.770 --> 00:12:32.770
You ate the rotten food, didn't you?

00:12:32.770 --> 00:12:35.020
No, I didn't.

00:12:35.020 --> 00:12:35.940
What about this?

00:12:35.940 --> 00:12:38.270
I'm not that awful.

00:12:39.780 --> 00:12:42.400
What are you talking about? That's Gargoyle's canned food!

00:12:42.400 --> 00:12:46.870
I'm not so awful that I'd eat Gargoyle's food!

00:12:47.990 --> 00:12:49.910
That's funny...

00:12:49.910 --> 00:12:53.120
There's nobody on this island except us, and maybe some monkeys.

00:12:57.210 --> 00:13:00.960
I see now. I was caught in Gargoyle's trap.

00:13:06.430 --> 00:13:10.010
My old friend, Nemo, may you rest in peace.

00:13:10.010 --> 00:13:17.190
You will remain far below the heavens, forever beyond our reach.

00:13:17.810 --> 00:13:21.820
The only light given to you will be...

00:13:21.820 --> 00:13:23.860
...the fires of Hell!

00:13:24.490 --> 00:13:28.780
The only pleasure given to you will be...

00:13:28.780 --> 00:13:30.740
...the agony of Hell!

00:13:30.740 --> 00:13:35.210
For the many brutal acts you've committed against us,

00:13:35.210 --> 00:13:39.210
you must suffer forever in the pits of Hell!

00:13:39.590 --> 00:13:41.670
It is the law of the universe!

00:13:42.550 --> 00:13:50.350
I will call this day "Nemo's Day" in remembrance of our pleasure.

00:13:53.890 --> 00:13:57.060
We have just one dream left!

00:13:57.520 --> 00:13:59.520
To whom does this Earth belong?

00:13:59.520 --> 00:14:01.690
Neo Atlantis!

00:14:01.940 --> 00:14:03.650
Beyond a doubt!

00:14:03.650 --> 00:14:10.530
We will begin a new operation in order to take over the Earth!

00:14:10.780 --> 00:14:14.790
The restoration of the Holy Fortress, Red Noah!

00:14:15.620 --> 00:14:21.590
It will carry us up to the heavens, to the very reaches of outer space!

00:14:21.590 --> 00:14:23.920
When it is restored, the ignorant human beings

00:14:23.920 --> 00:14:28.800
shall cast themselves down before the power of Neo Atlantis.

00:14:35.970 --> 00:14:38.690
You shouldn't have eaten that rotten food.

00:14:39.100 --> 00:14:41.650
You're wrong! It was a trap by Gargoyle!

00:14:41.650 --> 00:14:46.110
He must have floated the poisoned cans of food ashore aiming at us.

00:14:46.110 --> 00:14:51.570
If so, Gargoyle must not have used the fatal type of poison.

00:14:51.570 --> 00:14:55.870
It was just an old can of food, and you ate it because you were hungry.

00:14:55.870 --> 00:14:57.540
You sure are greedy, Nadia.

00:14:57.540 --> 00:15:00.750
You should have eaten with us.

00:15:00.750 --> 00:15:04.500
No thanks! I'd rather have stomach trouble from eating rotten food

00:15:04.500 --> 00:15:08.170
than ever eat an animal's dead body!

00:15:09.220 --> 00:15:10.880
You're so stubborn.

00:15:10.880 --> 00:15:13.550
Do you have loose bowels, Nadia?

00:15:13.550 --> 00:15:14.930
Do you have a fever?

00:15:14.930 --> 00:15:16.140
I'm all right.

00:15:16.140 --> 00:15:17.600
Let me see.

00:15:18.350 --> 00:15:19.390
You have a fever!

00:15:19.690 --> 00:15:21.190
It's nothing!

00:15:21.650 --> 00:15:24.770
Just a second, I may find a way to cure it.

00:15:26.610 --> 00:15:28.780
Never mind! I'll stay quiet and get better.

00:15:30.200 --> 00:15:31.990
Okay, stay here.

00:15:38.950 --> 00:15:42.420
You must stay here and take care of Nadia.

00:15:42.420 --> 00:15:44.170
Marie wants to go too!

00:15:44.170 --> 00:15:50.300
You can't! Nadia might eat more rotten food. You must watch her.

00:15:50.300 --> 00:15:52.970
King will take care of her!

00:15:52.970 --> 00:15:56.680
No! We don't know what might happen in the jungle.

00:15:56.680 --> 00:15:58.680
You must stay here!

00:15:58.680 --> 00:16:00.140
See you!

00:16:03.600 --> 00:16:06.110
Geez, this is no fun.

00:16:08.150 --> 00:16:09.900
Jean!

00:16:16.450 --> 00:16:18.950
Wait, please don't go.

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:36.550
Why? Why do you have to kill him?

00:16:37.720 --> 00:16:39.930
It isn't something I want to do.

00:16:39.930 --> 00:16:43.690
He hurt you because of his sickness.

00:16:43.690 --> 00:16:47.060
But Popo is my friend!

00:16:47.060 --> 00:16:51.650
If I must choose between the two of you, I'll take you, Nadia.

00:16:52.070 --> 00:16:54.360
We can't help what must be done.

00:16:54.780 --> 00:16:58.080
He can die peacefully with this medicine we use.

00:16:58.080 --> 00:17:00.830
It's better for him this way too.

00:17:01.540 --> 00:17:06.750
No! Don't do it! Don't kill him!

00:17:06.880 --> 00:17:08.590
No!

00:17:08.790 --> 00:17:14.880
Popo! Popo! Popo!

00:17:25.020 --> 00:17:30.570
Darn it. I can't find any good herbs because of the long drought.

00:17:37.450 --> 00:17:39.370
That frightened me!

00:17:39.370 --> 00:17:40.830
Jean!

00:17:43.330 --> 00:17:44.000
Marie!

00:17:44.000 --> 00:17:44.960
Jean!

00:17:44.960 --> 00:17:49.210
I thought I told you to stay home. It's very dangerous out here.

00:17:49.210 --> 00:17:51.250
It was too scary.

00:17:51.250 --> 00:17:52.670
Oh, geez.

00:17:55.550 --> 00:17:57.130
Hey, Jean.

00:17:58.800 --> 00:18:00.850
Am I bothering you?

00:18:02.430 --> 00:18:05.310
You'd rather have Nadia along, wouldn't you?

00:18:06.020 --> 00:18:08.100
Don't be so precocious.

00:18:19.820 --> 00:18:21.490
Please forgive me.

00:18:22.830 --> 00:18:24.080
Walk!

00:18:25.160 --> 00:18:26.870
Don't look down!

00:18:28.790 --> 00:18:30.210
Walk!

00:18:30.750 --> 00:18:34.760
I said walk, you good-for-nothing!

00:18:40.680 --> 00:18:44.390
You did well today. So I'm giving you this.

00:18:44.390 --> 00:18:46.480
You love this food, don't you?

00:18:47.890 --> 00:18:49.350
Are you scared of me?

00:18:49.350 --> 00:18:53.690
I scold you in order to prevent you from getting hurt.

00:18:54.320 --> 00:18:57.990
It doesn't mean I don't like you.

00:19:04.530 --> 00:19:07.040
I didn't know there was a place like this.

00:19:07.040 --> 00:19:09.370
This island is larger than I expected.

00:19:09.370 --> 00:19:11.750
I'm scared of this cave.

00:19:12.250 --> 00:19:14.420
You're a scaredy-cat, Marie.

00:19:16.300 --> 00:19:19.050
I'm just scared of this place.

00:19:19.050 --> 00:19:20.930
Wait here.

00:19:20.930 --> 00:19:25.560
There might be herbs in a damp place like this.

00:19:25.850 --> 00:19:28.310
Hurry back, please.

00:19:32.980 --> 00:19:36.190
I feel something gloomy.

00:19:39.190 --> 00:19:42.610
I can't see anything. It's too dark.

00:19:42.610 --> 00:19:45.530
I wish I had a flashlight.

00:19:53.460 --> 00:19:57.800
Jean, it stopped raining!

00:20:03.760 --> 00:20:08.850
I can't find it, maybe it's an unknown kind of mushroom.

00:20:26.580 --> 00:20:32.660
I'm so hungry! Let's go back!

00:20:33.750 --> 00:20:35.250
Marie!

00:20:37.790 --> 00:20:42.920
It's delicious! Come here quickly, Marie!

00:20:49.350 --> 00:20:51.890
I've never eaten such delicious things!

00:20:57.610 --> 00:21:00.900
Hurray! So delicious!

00:21:05.860 --> 00:21:09.030
Jean, what are you doing?

00:21:13.500 --> 00:21:15.870
Is this the main dish?

00:21:18.040 --> 00:21:19.170
What?

00:21:19.170 --> 00:21:22.130
It looks so delicious!

00:21:22.300 --> 00:21:24.260
Jean, you jerk!

00:21:27.550 --> 00:21:31.060
I'm not good to eat!

00:21:31.060 --> 00:21:34.140
I must brush my teeth after meals.

00:21:38.360 --> 00:21:40.650
Horses are good to eat.

00:21:40.650 --> 00:21:44.320
Geez, he's such a troublesome guy.

00:21:44.320 --> 00:21:47.160
It's hard to bite turtle's meat.

00:21:47.160 --> 00:21:48.870
Because of those mushrooms?

00:21:48.870 --> 00:21:51.240
Did you like the crabmeat so much?

00:21:51.240 --> 00:21:53.950
He should be the one to take care of me.

00:21:53.950 --> 00:21:58.960
You're saying he became like this trying to find an herb for me?

00:21:59.290 --> 00:22:02.170
I must take medicine and sleep well.

00:22:02.170 --> 00:22:07.430
That Jean! He said I looked plump and delicious!

00:22:07.430 --> 00:22:08.840
For me...

00:22:09.260 --> 00:22:10.970
He's awful, isn't he?

00:22:10.970 --> 00:22:13.180
Thank you, Jean!

00:22:13.640 --> 00:22:15.930
There are ten ants!

00:22:15.930 --> 00:22:18.520
This isn't right!

00:22:18.520 --> 00:22:21.150
Cows go moo.

00:22:27.860 --> 00:22:28.990
Say, Jean.

00:22:28.990 --> 00:22:30.660
Rocque Raltique.

00:22:31.240 --> 00:22:37.290
I had a dream. In it I realized that man cannot live alone.

00:22:37.290 --> 00:22:41.750
I never really thought about it before.

00:22:42.090 --> 00:22:45.800
Nadia's dream was very nice.

00:22:45.800 --> 00:22:51.430
In my dream I believed I could live all alone,

00:22:51.430 --> 00:22:56.390
and I thought I never had to ask anybody for help.

00:22:56.390 --> 00:22:59.730
It's difficult to talk about the past.

00:23:00.310 --> 00:23:05.190
But living on this desert island, I have learned for the first time

00:23:05.650 --> 00:23:10.160
the true meaning of one for all and all for one.

00:23:10.740 --> 00:23:14.620
I can live, helped by everyone.

00:23:14.620 --> 00:23:19.620
As long as there is somebody thinking about me.

00:23:19.620 --> 00:23:23.460
As long as there is someone worrying about me.

00:23:24.340 --> 00:23:27.340
Heavier than expected...

00:23:27.340 --> 00:23:30.800
Take me to Africa someday, okay?

00:23:30.800 --> 00:23:33.180
Africa is so...

00:23:33.430 --> 00:23:35.810
Stop talking, Jean.

00:23:39.850 --> 00:23:41.770
Take your glasses off.

00:23:41.770 --> 00:23:45.270
I can't see anything if I take them off.

00:23:45.770 --> 00:23:48.440
Stay with me forever.
